    Hover and focus effects are done in JavaScript for the same reason.
  - Every property is set explicitly so the LMS or template stylesheet
    can't restyle the buttons, fieldset or labels.
  - The fieldset's legend is visually hidden; the visible question is a
    paragraph linked with aria-describedby, which avoids the legend "notch".
  - The real radio buttons are visually hidden, not removed, so keyboards and
    screen readers still use them. The visible circles are drawn with spans.
  - Start Over clears the drawn circles itself, because form.reset()
